[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186179656 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0" "question-a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179511 :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y = \\dfrac{1}{x} - 2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/ff/ffd98b8f9b6c7a9260f43772f9c654901bd02c21efa1eb06f2a5fdad8b263729.png)\n\nSince we have $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}{\\color{red}\\,-\\,2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ *down* by $\\color{red}2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=\\dfrac 1 x$ is translated down by $2$ units, the horizontal asymptote $y=0$ is also translated down by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new horizontal asymptote is $y=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/b1/b157913f6fca24190330cdfa5c795e069eff15de8a2079d9e29e1d6e41b95cb4.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179657 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179512 :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x+2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/ff/ffd98b8f9b6c7a9260f43772f9c654901bd02c21efa1eb06f2a5fdad8b263729.png)\n\nSince we have $y = \\dfrac{1}{x \\color{red} + 2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ to the *left* by $\\color{red}2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y = \\dfrac 1 x$ is translated to the left by $2$ units, the vertical asymptote $x = 0$ is also translated to the left by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/e8/e8bff71235e67d8ad4046e94b5fe2682543674877a253ae6d4fe431504dbde3c.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179658 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179513 :question/problem "Plot the graph of $y=f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x-1}+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $\\color{red}-1$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *right*, and\n\n- the $\\color{blue}+2$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $2$ units *up*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/fe/fea5a705657b22621f3eb5ffe40cfcd59aef11036674d47e6d1f72e301d531f3.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0" :question/id #uuid "5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74372" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}-2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/1c/1cc1a1f5fa2bf98d700bf0c8d8e0630a4fda0540b8715865ee72d34b17049b8a.png)\n\nSince we have $y=-\\frac{1}{x}\\,-\\,2,$ we need to translate the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ *down* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated down by $2$ units, the horizontal asymptote $y=0$ is also translated down by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new horizontal asymptote is $y=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/10/10c52c6f400ff5880358c6653f2cd0341aed312317d88438a545b2522e19b61b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87" "answer-4b3f159b-1541-5e92-952b-f1551c9af726" "answer-a7b42cb5-47d2-5026-b8e6-267265a4d840" "answer-3375677f-2605-5437-aded-b6c2230d05ae" "answer-4c223c57-5e79-59f7-82f7-d42e3d82bde2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87" :answer/id #uuid "9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/10/10c52c6f400ff5880358c6653f2cd0341aed312317d88438a545b2522e19b61b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b3f159b-1541-5e92-952b-f1551c9af726" :answer/id #uuid "4b3f159b-1541-5e92-952b-f1551c9af726" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/56/56d343e13ae9af0bd1f204f82f11abc685aa0b33f627b8d1ad175be34814fba0.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7b42cb5-47d2-5026-b8e6-267265a4d840" :answer/id #uuid "a7b42cb5-47d2-5026-b8e6-267265a4d840" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/66/662f8c5ea9d851e9ba0b0fa5343a0dd0831b3d22745b24e1db138caadfcc51d2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3375677f-2605-5437-aded-b6c2230d05ae" :answer/id #uuid "3375677f-2605-5437-aded-b6c2230d05ae" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ac/ac83d9afe3a7c3333f9db674eee4458cfe5f210d58b5c48a5397b83be5fe103c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c223c57-5e79-59f7-82f7-d42e3d82bde2" :answer/id #uuid "4c223c57-5e79-59f7-82f7-d42e3d82bde2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fa/fa40fe0970b99770dfa6f228f4ed7b49db74d03c37162879b3458d83d340e7c1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28" :question/id #uuid "a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28" :question/math-academy-id "q-74370" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}+2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/1c/1cc1a1f5fa2bf98d700bf0c8d8e0630a4fda0540b8715865ee72d34b17049b8a.png)\n\nSince we have $y=-\\frac{1}{x}\\,+\\,2,$ we need to translate the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ *up* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated up by $2$ units, the horizontal asymptote $y=0$ is also translated up by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new horizontal asymptote is $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/fa/fa40fe0970b99770dfa6f228f4ed7b49db74d03c37162879b3458d83d340e7c1.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/id #uuid "73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92" :answer-field/choices ["answer-de0532c3-9ba6-579a-b169-217d96152121" "answer-f92d9fab-b888-55fb-a357-3b881cd30b6a" "answer-54c0b57c-a29e-5dd5-aff4-839755f093bd" "answer-90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92" "answer-0ff81a49-0d16-5746-903d-60f6f455bb68"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de0532c3-9ba6-579a-b169-217d96152121" :answer/id #uuid "de0532c3-9ba6-579a-b169-217d96152121" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/56/56d343e13ae9af0bd1f204f82f11abc685aa0b33f627b8d1ad175be34814fba0.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f92d9fab-b888-55fb-a357-3b881cd30b6a" :answer/id #uuid "f92d9fab-b888-55fb-a357-3b881cd30b6a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b8/b8ddc086b4a2a6e9f29843db6a861357271f14c138201ea314e6653ab51d1113.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54c0b57c-a29e-5dd5-aff4-839755f093bd" :answer/id #uuid "54c0b57c-a29e-5dd5-aff4-839755f093bd" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ca/ca3d18d029fb7a0111046704cc911d2f5027fc50a132ba456d987c1ded345ab2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92" :answer/id #uuid "90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fa/fa40fe0970b99770dfa6f228f4ed7b49db74d03c37162879b3458d83d340e7c1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ff81a49-0d16-5746-903d-60f6f455bb68" :answer/id #uuid "0ff81a49-0d16-5746-903d-60f6f455bb68" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fe/fe2430ab3ea16569aaba3c38e1d268f74cd7242c1e594eb5f14bc853b97a89e7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180265 :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/e3/e3f5ed500c81d09e2775f09fd10a221d7ec0fca7e39249b7add7a680328b68c1.png)\n\nSince we have $y=-\\frac{1}{x-2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ to the *right* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated to the right by $2$ units, the vertical asymptote $x=0$ is also translated to the right by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/c5/c575c9898d27a6bf612d89655fcb78328a25333088588de9a4c8fe54944c26aa.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179134 :answer-field/correct 17592186179138 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d" :question/id #uuid "cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74385" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/34/345fdaf3f301848b35448b710f240a308cfaadc1bae2729a5b0ddfa76793f6cb.png)\n\nSince we have $y=\\frac{1}{x-2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ to the *right* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated to the right by $2$ units, the vertical asymptote $x=0$ is also translated to the right by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/8e/8e73ed9744751224b9ef0bba78812f3681a9a98275f172b90552abcd1c6fc7d8.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d118d372-4320-5acc-bdd4-bcfef1d1a2d0" "answer-9030a799-cb3a-5ebf-9876-3b9560ccf0ab" "answer-227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794" "answer-485a3976-0372-5957-b2a8-bc15b2c010fa" "answer-3bc9ec70-cf1f-53e0-9fec-93b995dd44d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d118d372-4320-5acc-bdd4-bcfef1d1a2d0" :answer/id #uuid "d118d372-4320-5acc-bdd4-bcfef1d1a2d0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/12/12dffdcbf8105292d5d88f548ed673b214c2f491153c535e9749fe7e2e163d84.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9030a799-cb3a-5ebf-9876-3b9560ccf0ab" :answer/id #uuid "9030a799-cb3a-5ebf-9876-3b9560ccf0ab" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/2c/2ce69568487a3808d066cd0e0e3befb4732c3fb3125fab33e02d44bd8a309bdc.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794" :answer/id #uuid "227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/8e/8e73ed9744751224b9ef0bba78812f3681a9a98275f172b90552abcd1c6fc7d8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-485a3976-0372-5957-b2a8-bc15b2c010fa" :answer/id #uuid "485a3976-0372-5957-b2a8-bc15b2c010fa" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a1/a1d8f2f4b804c9a7b8998cfd27e84303b60e0ae215a0f126dfe4ff5bb43d97ca.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bc9ec70-cf1f-53e0-9fec-93b995dd44d5" :answer/id #uuid "3bc9ec70-cf1f-53e0-9fec-93b995dd44d5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b9/b9b68c4f4407add9b297d6a077c1cbef10d50f6d680678dd4190f4bd4a14e57d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180104 :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x+4}+2?$" :question/worked-solution "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $+4$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $4$ units to the *left*, and\n\n- the $+2$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $2$ units *up*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/85/851b90f3d442a528ccc2441f0c15e3ef344be9ee54c6789b312673a5ee7ae06f.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186178293 :answer-field/correct 17592186178295 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f" :question/id #uuid "8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-16354" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x+1}-3?$" :question/worked-solution "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $+1$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *left*, and\n\n- the $-3$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $3$ unit *down*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/b9/b9fd8ac22af99f7bd6f3afb039d58c4d2d790d6f9317de855c7f74fa4e5e2fd9.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/id #uuid "28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f20573f-00e1-5576-9906-d6b03bead2fd" "answer-421522a1-66e8-59b1-a216-2be4e4320260" "answer-121abf0e-8b53-58e9-8763-236faeb1d06c" "answer-4437a23e-22c3-5f0e-869a-2eddfe3b731a" "answer-b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f20573f-00e1-5576-9906-d6b03bead2fd" :answer/id #uuid "6f20573f-00e1-5576-9906-d6b03bead2fd" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/1d/1d7562a581959753faba29e0c5ab6fa44e5c8cae9664c2d039c255de04b9f368.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-421522a1-66e8-59b1-a216-2be4e4320260" :answer/id #uuid "421522a1-66e8-59b1-a216-2be4e4320260" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/54/545e45b986a627497e88fcd1b6b0b193f5875a55bfe30bf74d363dd3b3358ac3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-121abf0e-8b53-58e9-8763-236faeb1d06c" :answer/id #uuid "121abf0e-8b53-58e9-8763-236faeb1d06c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/93/9390ba26bd0e59509cd38bb0c01f77a12681595373498dec4af25e46a58d240c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4437a23e-22c3-5f0e-869a-2eddfe3b731a" :answer/id #uuid "4437a23e-22c3-5f0e-869a-2eddfe3b731a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b3/b3b27a72b3862acb9034ec0141009beda4e019d43f6abb6874a7be82632ca6d9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b" :answer/id #uuid "b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b9/b9fd8ac22af99f7bd6f3afb039d58c4d2d790d6f9317de855c7f74fa4e5e2fd9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180670 :tutorial/content "In general, the graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}+k\n$$\n\nis a vertical translation of the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by $k$ units up.\n\nFor example, to plot the function \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, {\\color{blue} \\, +\\, 2},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve *up* by $\\color{blue}2$ units:\n\n![](images/2a/2aa8f50f8a40719e237c0e3d3706a3e161bfe1b107f6639c1df1a9aa8a956cbf.png)\n\nSimilarly, to plot the function \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, {\\color{red} - \\, 3},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve *down* by $\\color{red}3$ units:\n\n![](images/45/45b81796c0140f9963afc26d13af1df9c9ac3f41de430f0dfee1192ab33bf42d.png)\n\nWith vertical translations of the reciprocal function, the vertical asymptote doesn't change, but the horizontal asymptote is translated by the same number of units." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180673 :tutorial/content "We also know the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x},$ so we can plot vertical translations of this function as well.\n\nFor example, to plot the function \n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, {\\color{blue} \\, +\\, 1.5},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve *up* by $\\color{blue}1.5$ units:\n\n![](images/01/0189d3fe1630049f5b4c7b1c13b134cc77454008e51450db5bf8d85b2050eeb8.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180671 :tutorial/content "Because we know how to plot the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x},$ we can also plot horizontal translations of this graph. In general, the graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x-h}\n$$\n\nis a horizontal translation of the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by $h$ units *right*.\n\nFor example, to plot the graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x {\\color{blue} \\, - \\, 1}},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve horizontally by $\\color{blue}1$ unit *right*:\n\n![](images/d4/d4778ef277b11ab33eb01a650ad07c4fd2e3902f303dd2fb15ed81a4b54649a0.png)\n\nThe graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x+h}\n$$\n\nis a horizontal translation of the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by $h$ units *left*.\n\nFor example, to plot the graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x{\\color{red} \\, + \\, 3}},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve by $\\color{red}3$ units *left*:\n\n![](images/87/87bbb7c00e10db814c9fc67786940cf5891d96496a2e85ed7ee2023bb1af8e3d.png)\n\n**Watch out!** Horizontal translations are always counter-intuitive. The translation $y=\\dfrac{1}{x-h}$ is to the right and the translation $y=\\dfrac{1}{x+h}$ is to the left, even though it seems like it should be the other way around.\n\nWith horizontal translations of the reciprocal function, the horizontal asymptote doesn't change, but the vertical asymptote is translated by the same number of units." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180672 :tutorial/content "We can combine horizontal and vertical translations of reciprocal functions.\n\nIn general, the graph of \n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{1}{x-h} + k\n$$\n\nis obtained from the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by translating it\n\n- horizontally by $h$ units to the right, and\n\n- vertically by $k$ units up.\n\nThe same is true regarding translations of the negative reciprocal function. In general, the graph of\n\n$$\ny = -\\dfrac{1}{x-h} + k\n$$\n\nis obtained from the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by translating it\n\n- horizontally by $h$ units to the right, and\n\n- vertically by $k$ units up." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179883 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186179511 :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y = \\dfrac{1}{x} - 2.$"] [17592186179511 :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/ff/ffd98b8f9b6c7a9260f43772f9c654901bd02c21efa1eb06f2a5fdad8b263729.png)\n\nSince we have $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}{\\color{red}\\,-\\,2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ *down* by $\\color{red}2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=\\dfrac 1 x$ is translated down by $2$ units, the horizontal asymptote $y=0$ is also translated down by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new horizontal asymptote is $y=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/b1/b157913f6fca24190330cdfa5c795e069eff15de8a2079d9e29e1d6e41b95cb4.png)"] [17592186179512 :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x+2}.$"] [17592186179512 :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/ff/ffd98b8f9b6c7a9260f43772f9c654901bd02c21efa1eb06f2a5fdad8b263729.png)\n\nSince we have $y = \\dfrac{1}{x \\color{red} + 2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ to the *left* by $\\color{red}2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y = \\dfrac 1 x$ is translated to the left by $2$ units, the vertical asymptote $x = 0$ is also translated to the left by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/e8/e8bff71235e67d8ad4046e94b5fe2682543674877a253ae6d4fe431504dbde3c.png)"] [17592186179513 :question/problem "Plot the graph of $y=f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x-1}+2.$"] [17592186179513 :question/worked-solution "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $\\color{red}-1$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *right*, and\n\n- the $\\color{blue}+2$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $2$ units *up*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/fe/fea5a705657b22621f3eb5ffe40cfcd59aef11036674d47e6d1f72e301d531f3.png)"] ["question-5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0" :question/id #uuid "5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0"] ["question-5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74372"] ["question-5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}-2?$"] ["question-5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/1c/1cc1a1f5fa2bf98d700bf0c8d8e0630a4fda0540b8715865ee72d34b17049b8a.png)\n\nSince we have $y=-\\frac{1}{x}\\,-\\,2,$ we need to translate the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ *down* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated down by $2$ units, the horizontal asymptote $y=0$ is also translated down by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new horizontal asymptote is $y=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/10/10c52c6f400ff5880358c6653f2cd0341aed312317d88438a545b2522e19b61b.png)"] ["question-5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8"] ["answer-9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87" :answer/id #uuid "9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87"] ["answer-9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87" :answer/value "images/10/10c52c6f400ff5880358c6653f2cd0341aed312317d88438a545b2522e19b61b.png"] ["answer-4b3f159b-1541-5e92-952b-f1551c9af726" :answer/id #uuid "4b3f159b-1541-5e92-952b-f1551c9af726"] ["answer-4b3f159b-1541-5e92-952b-f1551c9af726" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-4b3f159b-1541-5e92-952b-f1551c9af726" :answer/value "images/56/56d343e13ae9af0bd1f204f82f11abc685aa0b33f627b8d1ad175be34814fba0.png"] ["answer-a7b42cb5-47d2-5026-b8e6-267265a4d840" :answer/id #uuid "a7b42cb5-47d2-5026-b8e6-267265a4d840"] ["answer-a7b42cb5-47d2-5026-b8e6-267265a4d840" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-a7b42cb5-47d2-5026-b8e6-267265a4d840" :answer/value "images/66/662f8c5ea9d851e9ba0b0fa5343a0dd0831b3d22745b24e1db138caadfcc51d2.png"] ["answer-3375677f-2605-5437-aded-b6c2230d05ae" :answer/id #uuid "3375677f-2605-5437-aded-b6c2230d05ae"] ["answer-3375677f-2605-5437-aded-b6c2230d05ae" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-3375677f-2605-5437-aded-b6c2230d05ae" :answer/value "images/ac/ac83d9afe3a7c3333f9db674eee4458cfe5f210d58b5c48a5397b83be5fe103c.png"] ["answer-4c223c57-5e79-59f7-82f7-d42e3d82bde2" :answer/id #uuid "4c223c57-5e79-59f7-82f7-d42e3d82bde2"] ["answer-4c223c57-5e79-59f7-82f7-d42e3d82bde2" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-4c223c57-5e79-59f7-82f7-d42e3d82bde2" :answer/value "images/fa/fa40fe0970b99770dfa6f228f4ed7b49db74d03c37162879b3458d83d340e7c1.png"] ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/correct "answer-9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87"] ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/choices "answer-9b71c6d8-23d9-5cfc-a5fb-af31bdaa4b87"] ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/choices "answer-4b3f159b-1541-5e92-952b-f1551c9af726"] ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/choices "answer-a7b42cb5-47d2-5026-b8e6-267265a4d840"] ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/choices "answer-3375677f-2605-5437-aded-b6c2230d05ae"] ["answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8" :answer-field/choices "answer-4c223c57-5e79-59f7-82f7-d42e3d82bde2"] ["question-5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-ac7ab396-9bb4-5f64-be8c-3f934bdab4d8"] [17592186179656 :knowledge-point/questions "question-5828ff13-ff61-55c4-8b7d-7147118b03b0"] ["question-a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28" :question/id #uuid "a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28"] ["question-a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28" :question/math-academy-id "q-74370"] ["question-a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}+2?$"] ["question-a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/1c/1cc1a1f5fa2bf98d700bf0c8d8e0630a4fda0540b8715865ee72d34b17049b8a.png)\n\nSince we have $y=-\\frac{1}{x}\\,+\\,2,$ we need to translate the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ *up* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated up by $2$ units, the horizontal asymptote $y=0$ is also translated up by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new horizontal asymptote is $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/fa/fa40fe0970b99770dfa6f228f4ed7b49db74d03c37162879b3458d83d340e7c1.png)"] ["question-a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/id #uuid "73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b"] ["answer-de0532c3-9ba6-579a-b169-217d96152121" :answer/id #uuid "de0532c3-9ba6-579a-b169-217d96152121"] ["answer-de0532c3-9ba6-579a-b169-217d96152121" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-de0532c3-9ba6-579a-b169-217d96152121" :answer/value "images/56/56d343e13ae9af0bd1f204f82f11abc685aa0b33f627b8d1ad175be34814fba0.png"] ["answer-f92d9fab-b888-55fb-a357-3b881cd30b6a" :answer/id #uuid "f92d9fab-b888-55fb-a357-3b881cd30b6a"] ["answer-f92d9fab-b888-55fb-a357-3b881cd30b6a" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-f92d9fab-b888-55fb-a357-3b881cd30b6a" :answer/value "images/b8/b8ddc086b4a2a6e9f29843db6a861357271f14c138201ea314e6653ab51d1113.png"] ["answer-54c0b57c-a29e-5dd5-aff4-839755f093bd" :answer/id #uuid "54c0b57c-a29e-5dd5-aff4-839755f093bd"] ["answer-54c0b57c-a29e-5dd5-aff4-839755f093bd" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-54c0b57c-a29e-5dd5-aff4-839755f093bd" :answer/value "images/ca/ca3d18d029fb7a0111046704cc911d2f5027fc50a132ba456d987c1ded345ab2.png"] ["answer-90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92" :answer/id #uuid "90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92"] ["answer-90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92" :answer/value "images/fa/fa40fe0970b99770dfa6f228f4ed7b49db74d03c37162879b3458d83d340e7c1.png"] ["answer-0ff81a49-0d16-5746-903d-60f6f455bb68" :answer/id #uuid "0ff81a49-0d16-5746-903d-60f6f455bb68"] ["answer-0ff81a49-0d16-5746-903d-60f6f455bb68" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-0ff81a49-0d16-5746-903d-60f6f455bb68" :answer/value "images/fe/fe2430ab3ea16569aaba3c38e1d268f74cd7242c1e594eb5f14bc853b97a89e7.png"] ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/correct "answer-90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92"] ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-de0532c3-9ba6-579a-b169-217d96152121"] ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-f92d9fab-b888-55fb-a357-3b881cd30b6a"] ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-54c0b57c-a29e-5dd5-aff4-839755f093bd"] ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-90cffb8a-d87b-5902-a447-970ea110de92"] ["answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-0ff81a49-0d16-5746-903d-60f6f455bb68"] ["question-a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-73b8b396-f960-5434-9408-2683ac668e9b"] [17592186179656 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a049f227-9a74-52c4-a177-20bed5af6f28"] [17592186180265 :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x-2}.$"] [17592186180265 :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/e3/e3f5ed500c81d09e2775f09fd10a221d7ec0fca7e39249b7add7a680328b68c1.png)\n\nSince we have $y=-\\frac{1}{x-2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ to the *right* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated to the right by $2$ units, the vertical asymptote $x=0$ is also translated to the right by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/c5/c575c9898d27a6bf612d89655fcb78328a25333088588de9a4c8fe54944c26aa.png)"] [17592186180265 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186179134 :answer-field/correct 17592186179138] ["question-cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d" :question/id #uuid "cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d"] ["question-cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74385"] ["question-cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x-2}.$"] ["question-cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/34/345fdaf3f301848b35448b710f240a308cfaadc1bae2729a5b0ddfa76793f6cb.png)\n\nSince we have $y=\\frac{1}{x-2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ to the *right* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated to the right by $2$ units, the vertical asymptote $x=0$ is also translated to the right by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/8e/8e73ed9744751224b9ef0bba78812f3681a9a98275f172b90552abcd1c6fc7d8.png)"] ["question-cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a"] ["answer-d118d372-4320-5acc-bdd4-bcfef1d1a2d0" :answer/id #uuid "d118d372-4320-5acc-bdd4-bcfef1d1a2d0"] ["answer-d118d372-4320-5acc-bdd4-bcfef1d1a2d0" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-d118d372-4320-5acc-bdd4-bcfef1d1a2d0" :answer/value "images/12/12dffdcbf8105292d5d88f548ed673b214c2f491153c535e9749fe7e2e163d84.png"] ["answer-9030a799-cb3a-5ebf-9876-3b9560ccf0ab" :answer/id #uuid "9030a799-cb3a-5ebf-9876-3b9560ccf0ab"] ["answer-9030a799-cb3a-5ebf-9876-3b9560ccf0ab" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-9030a799-cb3a-5ebf-9876-3b9560ccf0ab" :answer/value "images/2c/2ce69568487a3808d066cd0e0e3befb4732c3fb3125fab33e02d44bd8a309bdc.png"] ["answer-227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794" :answer/id #uuid "227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794"] ["answer-227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794" :answer/value "images/8e/8e73ed9744751224b9ef0bba78812f3681a9a98275f172b90552abcd1c6fc7d8.png"] ["answer-485a3976-0372-5957-b2a8-bc15b2c010fa" :answer/id #uuid "485a3976-0372-5957-b2a8-bc15b2c010fa"] ["answer-485a3976-0372-5957-b2a8-bc15b2c010fa" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-485a3976-0372-5957-b2a8-bc15b2c010fa" :answer/value "images/a1/a1d8f2f4b804c9a7b8998cfd27e84303b60e0ae215a0f126dfe4ff5bb43d97ca.png"] ["answer-3bc9ec70-cf1f-53e0-9fec-93b995dd44d5" :answer/id #uuid "3bc9ec70-cf1f-53e0-9fec-93b995dd44d5"] ["answer-3bc9ec70-cf1f-53e0-9fec-93b995dd44d5" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-3bc9ec70-cf1f-53e0-9fec-93b995dd44d5" :answer/value "images/b9/b9b68c4f4407add9b297d6a077c1cbef10d50f6d680678dd4190f4bd4a14e57d.png"] ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/correct "answer-227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794"] ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/choices "answer-d118d372-4320-5acc-bdd4-bcfef1d1a2d0"] ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/choices "answer-9030a799-cb3a-5ebf-9876-3b9560ccf0ab"] ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/choices "answer-227aed43-5c3b-549b-b3c8-0cd389937794"] ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/choices "answer-485a3976-0372-5957-b2a8-bc15b2c010fa"] ["answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a" :answer-field/choices "answer-3bc9ec70-cf1f-53e0-9fec-93b995dd44d5"] ["question-cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f0b86c36-4ba5-5460-9bef-164231b9026a"] [17592186179657 :knowledge-point/questions "question-cdddff3e-12b7-51e5-bbd8-54acd953d28d"] [17592186180104 :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x+4}+2?$"] [17592186180104 :question/worked-solution "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $+4$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $4$ units to the *left*, and\n\n- the $+2$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $2$ units *up*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/85/851b90f3d442a528ccc2441f0c15e3ef344be9ee54c6789b312673a5ee7ae06f.png)"] [17592186180104 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186178293 :answer-field/correct 17592186178295] ["question-8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f" :question/id #uuid "8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f"] ["question-8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-16354"] ["question-8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x+1}-3?$"] ["question-8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f" :question/worked-solution "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $+1$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *left*, and\n\n- the $-3$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $3$ unit *down*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/b9/b9fd8ac22af99f7bd6f3afb039d58c4d2d790d6f9317de855c7f74fa4e5e2fd9.png)"] ["question-8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/id #uuid "28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467"] ["answer-6f20573f-00e1-5576-9906-d6b03bead2fd" :answer/id #uuid "6f20573f-00e1-5576-9906-d6b03bead2fd"] ["answer-6f20573f-00e1-5576-9906-d6b03bead2fd" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-6f20573f-00e1-5576-9906-d6b03bead2fd" :answer/value "images/1d/1d7562a581959753faba29e0c5ab6fa44e5c8cae9664c2d039c255de04b9f368.png"] ["answer-421522a1-66e8-59b1-a216-2be4e4320260" :answer/id #uuid "421522a1-66e8-59b1-a216-2be4e4320260"] ["answer-421522a1-66e8-59b1-a216-2be4e4320260" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-421522a1-66e8-59b1-a216-2be4e4320260" :answer/value "images/54/545e45b986a627497e88fcd1b6b0b193f5875a55bfe30bf74d363dd3b3358ac3.png"] ["answer-121abf0e-8b53-58e9-8763-236faeb1d06c" :answer/id #uuid "121abf0e-8b53-58e9-8763-236faeb1d06c"] ["answer-121abf0e-8b53-58e9-8763-236faeb1d06c" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-121abf0e-8b53-58e9-8763-236faeb1d06c" :answer/value "images/93/9390ba26bd0e59509cd38bb0c01f77a12681595373498dec4af25e46a58d240c.png"] ["answer-4437a23e-22c3-5f0e-869a-2eddfe3b731a" :answer/id #uuid "4437a23e-22c3-5f0e-869a-2eddfe3b731a"] ["answer-4437a23e-22c3-5f0e-869a-2eddfe3b731a" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-4437a23e-22c3-5f0e-869a-2eddfe3b731a" :answer/value "images/b3/b3b27a72b3862acb9034ec0141009beda4e019d43f6abb6874a7be82632ca6d9.png"] ["answer-b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b" :answer/id #uuid "b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b"] ["answer-b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b" :answer/value "images/b9/b9fd8ac22af99f7bd6f3afb039d58c4d2d790d6f9317de855c7f74fa4e5e2fd9.png"] ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/correct "answer-b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b"] ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/choices "answer-6f20573f-00e1-5576-9906-d6b03bead2fd"] ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/choices "answer-421522a1-66e8-59b1-a216-2be4e4320260"] ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/choices "answer-121abf0e-8b53-58e9-8763-236faeb1d06c"] ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/choices "answer-4437a23e-22c3-5f0e-869a-2eddfe3b731a"] ["answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467" :answer-field/choices "answer-b09332fe-56fa-5587-b530-d218abf10c5b"] ["question-8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-28b0dca8-0e92-54e9-8055-2a7b0fae2467"] [17592186179658 :knowledge-point/questions "question-8042fdd6-a329-5d96-ab3c-3d93ab337f8f"] [17592186180670 :tutorial/content "In general, the graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}+k\n$$\n\nis a vertical translation of the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by $k$ units up.\n\nFor example, to plot the function \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, {\\color{blue} \\, +\\, 2},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve *up* by $\\color{blue}2$ units:\n\n![](images/2a/2aa8f50f8a40719e237c0e3d3706a3e161bfe1b107f6639c1df1a9aa8a956cbf.png)\n\nSimilarly, to plot the function \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, {\\color{red} - \\, 3},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve *down* by $\\color{red}3$ units:\n\n![](images/45/45b81796c0140f9963afc26d13af1df9c9ac3f41de430f0dfee1192ab33bf42d.png)\n\nWith vertical translations of the reciprocal function, the vertical asymptote doesn't change, but the horizontal asymptote is translated by the same number of units."] [17592186180673 :tutorial/content "We also know the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x},$ so we can plot vertical translations of this function as well.\n\nFor example, to plot the function \n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, {\\color{blue} \\, +\\, 1.5},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve *up* by $\\color{blue}1.5$ units:\n\n![](images/01/0189d3fe1630049f5b4c7b1c13b134cc77454008e51450db5bf8d85b2050eeb8.png)"] [17592186180671 :tutorial/content "Because we know how to plot the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x},$ we can also plot horizontal translations of this graph. In general, the graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x-h}\n$$\n\nis a horizontal translation of the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by $h$ units *right*.\n\nFor example, to plot the graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x {\\color{blue} \\, - \\, 1}},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve horizontally by $\\color{blue}1$ unit *right*:\n\n![](images/d4/d4778ef277b11ab33eb01a650ad07c4fd2e3902f303dd2fb15ed81a4b54649a0.png)\n\nThe graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x+h}\n$$\n\nis a horizontal translation of the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by $h$ units *left*.\n\nFor example, to plot the graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x{\\color{red} \\, + \\, 3}},\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve by $\\color{red}3$ units *left*:\n\n![](images/87/87bbb7c00e10db814c9fc67786940cf5891d96496a2e85ed7ee2023bb1af8e3d.png)\n\n**Watch out!** Horizontal translations are always counter-intuitive. The translation $y=\\dfrac{1}{x-h}$ is to the right and the translation $y=\\dfrac{1}{x+h}$ is to the left, even though it seems like it should be the other way around.\n\nWith horizontal translations of the reciprocal function, the horizontal asymptote doesn't change, but the vertical asymptote is translated by the same number of units."] [17592186180672 :tutorial/content "We can combine horizontal and vertical translations of reciprocal functions.\n\nIn general, the graph of \n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{1}{x-h} + k\n$$\n\nis obtained from the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by translating it\n\n- horizontally by $h$ units to the right, and\n\n- vertically by $k$ units up.\n\nThe same is true regarding translations of the negative reciprocal function. In general, the graph of\n\n$$\ny = -\\dfrac{1}{x-h} + k\n$$\n\nis obtained from the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}$ by translating it\n\n- horizontally by $h$ units to the right, and\n\n- vertically by $k$ units up."] [17592186179883 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0]] "retractions" [[17592186179511 :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y = \\dfrac{1}{x} - 2$."] [17592186179511 :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\n![](images/ff/ffd98b8f9b6c7a9260f43772f9c654901bd02c21efa1eb06f2a5fdad8b263729.png)\n\nSince we have\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}{\\color{red}\\,-\\,2}\n$$\n\nwe need to translate the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\n*down* by $\\color{red}2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac 1 x\n$$\n\nis translated down by $2$ units, the horizontal asymptote $y=0$ is also translated down by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new horizontal asymptote is $y=-2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/b1/b157913f6fca24190330cdfa5c795e069eff15de8a2079d9e29e1d6e41b95cb4.png)"] [17592186179512 :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x+2}$."] [17592186179512 :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\n![](images/ff/ffd98b8f9b6c7a9260f43772f9c654901bd02c21efa1eb06f2a5fdad8b263729.png)\n\nSince we have\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{1}{x \\color{red} + 2}\n$$\n\nwe need to translate the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nto the *left* by $\\color{red}2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac 1 x\n$$\n\nis translated to the left by $2$ units, the vertical asymptote $x = 0$ is also translated to the left by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=-2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/e8/e8bff71235e67d8ad4046e94b5fe2682543674877a253ae6d4fe431504dbde3c.png)"] [17592186179513 :question/problem "Plot the graph of $y=f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x-1}+2$."] [17592186179513 :question/worked-solution "The given function can be obtained by translating\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nboth horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $\\color{red}-1$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *right*, and\n- the $\\color{blue}+2$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $2$ units *up*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/fe/fea5a705657b22621f3eb5ffe40cfcd59aef11036674d47e6d1f72e301d531f3.png)"] [17592186180265 :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y =-\\frac{1}{x - 2}$."] [17592186180104 :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y = \\frac{1}{x + 4} + 2$?"] [17592186180670 :tutorial/content "In general, the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}+k\n$$\n\nis a vertical translation of the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nby $k$ units up.\n\nFor example, to plot the function\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, {\\color{blue} \\, +\\, 2}\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve *up* by $\\color{blue}2$ units:\n\n![](images/2a/2aa8f50f8a40719e237c0e3d3706a3e161bfe1b107f6639c1df1a9aa8a956cbf.png)\n\nSimilarly, to plot the function\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, {\\color{red} - \\, 3}\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve *down* by $\\color{red}3$ units:\n\n![](images/45/45b81796c0140f9963afc26d13af1df9c9ac3f41de430f0dfee1192ab33bf42d.png)\n\nWith vertical translations of the reciprocal function, the vertical asymptote doesn't change, but the horizontal asymptote is translated by the same number of units."] [17592186180673 :tutorial/content "We also know the graph of\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nso we can plot vertical translations of this function as well.\n\nFor example, to plot the function\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, {\\color{blue} \\, +\\, 1.5}\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve *up* by $\\color{blue}1.5$ units:\n\n![](images/01/0189d3fe1630049f5b4c7b1c13b134cc77454008e51450db5bf8d85b2050eeb8.png)"] [17592186180671 :tutorial/content "Because we know how to plot the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nwe can also plot horizontal translations of this graph. In general, the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x-h}\n$$\n\nis a horizontal translation of the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nby $h$ units *right*.\n\nFor example, to plot the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x {\\color{blue} \\,-\\, 1}}\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve horizontally by $\\color{blue}1$ unit *right*:\n\n![](images/d4/d4778ef277b11ab33eb01a650ad07c4fd2e3902f303dd2fb15ed81a4b54649a0.png)\n\nThe graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x+h}\n$$\n\nis a horizontal translation of the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nby $h$ units *left*.\n\nFor example, to plot the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x{\\color{red} \\, + \\, 3}}\n$$\n\nwe translate the original curve by $\\color{red}3$ units *left*:\n\n![](images/87/87bbb7c00e10db814c9fc67786940cf5891d96496a2e85ed7ee2023bb1af8e3d.png)\n\n**Watch out!** Horizontal translations are always counter-intuitive. The translation\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x-h}\n$$\n\nis to the right and the translation\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x+h}\n$$\n\nis to the left, even though it seems like it should be the other way around.\n\nWith horizontal translations of the reciprocal function, the horizontal asymptote doesn't change, but the vertical asymptote is translated by the same number of units."] [17592186180672 :tutorial/content "We can combine horizontal and vertical translations of reciprocal functions.\n\nIn general, the graph of\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{1}{x-h} + k\n$$\n\nis obtained from the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nby translating it\n\n- horizontally by $h$ units to the right, and\n- vertically by $k$ units up.\n\nThe same is true regarding translations of the negative reciprocal function. In general, the graph of\n\n$$\ny = -\\dfrac{1}{x-h} + k\n$$\n\nis obtained from the graph of\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nby translating it\n\n- horizontally by $h$ units to the right, and\n- vertically by $k$ units up."]]}]